usage: n88 FILE.bas
       n88 -

  Runs an N88-BASIC(86) program. Output goes to stdout; a program that
  draws also writes a PNG beside its source.

  "-" reads the program from stdin and draws into "n88.png" in the
  working directory. The program has then consumed stdin, so INPUT and
  LINE INPUT have nothing left to read and stop with "Out of input";
  pass a file when a program asks for input.

  --immediate, -i
              the manual's direct mode (printed pp.4-6): statements are
              read from stdin and executed as they arrive, and the
              variables they set persist. A line typed with a number in
              front is stored instead; RUN executes the stored lines, LIST
              shows them, a bare line number deletes one, and NEW erases
              the program. A session that draws writes "n88.png" when it
              ends.

  --uninstall remove this binary, and list what else came with n88
              (add --yes to skip the confirmation)
  --version   print the version and exit
  --help      print this message and exit
